    "mode": "hybrid",
    "results": [
      {
        "id": "d02",
        "text": "WebGPU exposes the device GPU for browser computation. An embedding application should request a GPU adapter and explicitly select the webgpu execution provider. FP16 operations require the shader-f16 adapter feature.",
        "metadata": {
          "chunk": 0,
          "model": "Xenova/all-MiniLM-L6-v2",
          "title": "WebGPU acceleration",
          "source": "WebGPU acceleration",
          "revision": "751bff37182d3f1213fa05d7196b954e230abad9"
        },
        "score": 0.0325
      },
      {
        "id": "d31",
        "text": "ONNX is a model interchange format. ONNX Runtime Web executes exported networks in browsers using WebGPU or WASM providers. Exported operator support must be checked on both backends before shipping an application.",
        "metadata": {
          "chunk": 0,
          "model": "Xenova/all-MiniLM-L6-v2",
          "title": "ONNX portability",
          "source": "ONNX portability",
          "revision": "751bff37182d3f1213fa05d7196b954e230abad9"
        },
        "score": 0.032
      },
      {
        "id": "d03",
        "text": "When no GPU adapter is available, an embedding application can use WebAssembly on the CPU. The interface should clearly show WASM as the active inference backend. INT8 models reduce download and memory cost.",
        "metadata": {
          "chunk": 0,
          "model": "Xenova/all-MiniLM-L6-v2",
          "title": "WASM fallback",
          "source": "WASM fallback",
          "revision": "751bff37182d3f1213fa05d7196b954e230abad9"
        },
        "score": 0.032
      },
      {
        "id": "d30",
        "text": "WASM threads can speed CPU inference when the page is cross-origin isolated. COOP and COEP headers enable SharedArrayBuffer in compatible browsers. Thread count should be recorded because it affects fair performance comparisons.",
        "metadata": {
          "chunk": 0,
          "model": "Xenova/all-MiniLM-L6-v2",
          "title": "CPU parallelism",
          "source": "CPU parallelism",
          "revision": "751bff37182d3f1213fa05d7196b954e230abad9"
        },
        "score": 0.0315
      },
      {
        "id": "d23",
        "text": "Browser caches avoid downloading model weights on every visit. Cache keys should include a pinned model revision to prevent stale artifacts from being mixed with new tokenizers. Clearing the browser cache makes a fresh download experiment reproducible.",
        "metadata": {
          "chunk": 0,
          "model": "Xenova/all-MiniLM-L6-v2",
          "title": "Cache management",
          "source": "Cache management",
          "revision": "751bff37182d3f1213fa05d7196b954e230abad9"
        },
        "score": 0.0154
      }
    ],
